== ARCHIVE: full 74-test suite run on the tree that carries the 2026-10-05 re-audit ==

    $ PYTHONUTF8=1 python3 -m pytest -q -rs      (WSL, python 3.10.12, pyscf 2.12.1, numpy 2.2.6,
      host <OPERATOR>, git HEAD 8906165ba2e6ea6840539fe18f529c54ee9fe51c + the uncommitted changes listed below)
    74 passed in 347.92s (0:05:47)
    EXIT=0

Why this run exists. The collection grew from the 69 tests of `20260930T233800Z_suite69_full.out`
to 74, and every one of those added tests is an invariant written during the 2026-10-05 re-audit
(the benzene geometry labels in `nlcsplit/tests/test_geometry.py`, the CC-convention and regression
rows that came in with the ghost-function fix). The paragraph in `paper/software.md` that said
"all 69 have been executed" was therefore about a tree that no longer exists; this archive is the
execution of the tree the paper now describes. The count itself is not taken from this file: it is
produced by `test_count_census.py` (`20261005T0404Z_test_count_census.out`: 74 collected, 53 non-slow
+ 21 slow), so the collection and the execution are two separate records.

The run is of the working tree, so the tree is named rather than asserted clean:

